        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "After using both phones for a while, we compared the crease on the Galaxy Z Fold 8 and the OPPO Find N6 again.\n\nThe result remains the same: the Galaxy Z Fold 8 is better. Its inner display is noticeably flatter, with a less visible crease.\n\nAs for the other foldables, there’s really no need to compare them anymore. They’ve already lost this battle.\n\nAt this point, I think we can confidently say that the Galaxy Z Fold 8 currently has the best crease-control solution in the smartphone industry.\n\nNow all eyes are on the iPhone Ultra. How will Apple deal with the crease? And more importantly, can it actually beat Samsung?"
        },
